### Absence checks performed (URL and result, 2026-11-12)

- `https://opencode.ai/docs/zen` — 200, **0 occurrences** of `owo` in the Zen model, pricing and deprecation tables.
- `https://opencode.ai/inference/v1/models` — 200, live inference catalogue, **no `owo` entry**.
- `https://models.dev/api.json` (whole catalogue, every provider) — 200, **0 occurrences** of `owo` (the same scan finds `muse-spark-open` and `muse-ember` rows, so the string search was working).
- `https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models` — 200, ~842 KB of catalogue, **0 occurrences** of `owo`.
- `https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1/models` — 200, ~569 KB of catalogue, **0 occurrences** of `owo`.
- Artificial Analysis catalogue (285 models, 2026-11-11 snapshot) — **no `owo` entry**; a live probe of `artificialanalysis.ai/models/owo-2-5` returns **HTTP 404**.
- `https://www.owo.ai/` — 200, OwO.AI's company page: "We build Human World Models", news entries through **Mar 2026** (wearable sensing platform in development), **no language-model release** at any point in the timeline.
- `https://owo.ai/developers/` — 200, the Developers page: Design System, API Reference and SDKs & Libraries all marked **"Coming Soon"**; no model ids, no endpoints, no prices.
- `https://owo.ai/research/` — 200, empty page body.
- `https://docs.owo.ai/` — **transport error** (host does not resolve / does not serve); no Owo API documentation is reachable.
- `https://huggingface.co/api/models?search=owo-2.5` — 200, **empty result array** (no weights, no repo).
- DuckDuckGo searches for `"Owo 2.5" LLM API pricing`, `"owo-2.5" OR "Owo 2.5" model benchmark`, `"Owo" AI model API 1M context multimodal September 2026 OpenCode`, and `owo.ai OR "Owo API" large language model 2026 OpenCode` — **no result describing an AI model of this name**; the hits are OwO.AI itself (an embodied-intelligence company whose developer pages are placeholders), an unrelated Rust "OwO AI Gateway" gateway tool on GitHub, Civitai image checkpoints tagged "owo", and a Chinese content creator.
- DuckDuckGo search in Chinese (`"Owo" 大模型 API 2.5 价格`) — no language-model result.

### Conflicting evidence (vendor vs independent) and how it was resolved

There is no vendor claim and no independent measurement to reconcile: no vendor statement exists, and no independent source has ever published a number for this id. The only conflict is between this repository's curated metadata (which asserts a September 2026 release, a 1M/256K window, text+image input, tool use and $0.40/$3.20 pricing "per official Owo API docs") and the complete absence of those specs — and of the API documentation they cite — from every public source checked. It was resolved by treating every curated specification as unverified metadata rather than as sourced fact, and by filing this report as evidence-free.

### Notes on identity

- **Publicly documented:** nothing beyond the name. There is no vendor model page, no API documentation, no announcement, no model card, no weights, no Hugging Face repository, no pricing row, no context-window row and no benchmark result for `owo-2.5` in any public catalogue checked on 2026-11-12.
- **Attribution-by-telemetry:** none. Unlike the other stealth entries in this dataset, there is not even a tokenizer or self-introduction lead — no community probe, tracker sighting or telemetry signal was found for this name.
- **Endpoint still live?** No endpoint was found. The id is absent from OpenCode's live inference catalogue, from the Zen/Console pricing and deprecation tables, from models.dev, from OpenRouter and from the Vercel AI Gateway catalogue, so the entry appears either never to have shipped, to have been withdrawn before any catalogue snapshot was taken, or to be a curated placeholder whose public trail is empty. The only name-matching company on the internet (OwO.AI) is building embodied "Human World Models" and has published no language model and no API.
- **Why this is a legitimate finding:** a documented absence is still a finding. Because there is no verified public benchmark number for this id, the sync pipeline quarantines this file on purpose — it is saved with the `.md.excluded` suffix so that no invented number can enter the averages.

### Normalized scores (1–100)

No scores are assigned for this entry. Every dimension of the rubric (tool use, reasoning, context window, multimodal, coding, cost efficiency) depends on a verified measurement or a documented catalogue row, and for `owo-2.5` none exists: the raw-benchmarks section above is entirely "no verified public score found". Publishing a scored file would mean inventing a benchmark or passing curated metadata off as sourced fact, so this file is intentionally saved as `MiniMax_M3.1_Flash.md.excluded` and contributes nothing to the averages.

